# Ask Before GitHub Operations

Never run GitHub operations without explicit user approval in the current conversation.

## Requires asking first

- Creating, updating, merging, or closing pull requests (`gh pr ...`)
- Pushing to remote (`git push`, including `-u`)
- Creating/deleting branches on remote
- Creating, editing, or closing GitHub issues
- Creating or modifying GitHub releases
- Changing repo settings, secrets, or collaborators via `gh`
- Forking, starring, or other GitHub API / `gh` mutations

## How to ask

Before any of the above, stop and ask clearly what you intend to do (e.g. "Push this branch and open a PR?"). Wait for an affirmative reply. Do not assume prior consent from another chat or from user rules that describe *how* to do GitHub work.

## Allowed without asking

- Read-only inspection: `gh pr view`, `gh pr list`, `gh issue list`, `git status`, `git log`, `git diff`, fetching remote status
- Local-only git that does not touch GitHub (commit only when the user asked to commit)
